## 7. Approach, samples, roles, acceptance

Negative gate tests, server-side binding controls, limited scripted tests, historical samples, automated MA-01; criteria and minimum samples: {{doc_id_02}}.

Planned: OQ-01, OQ-10 [fill in]; OQ-02 to OQ-07 [fill in: repositories]; MA-01 [fill in: ids]; PQ [fill in: period]. Sample rule (random, seed recorded): [fill in]. PQ-01 outlier: approval within [fill in: x] minutes of ready-for-review, or without comment, on a diff over [fill in: y] lines; reviewed by [fill in: qualified reviewer, not the approver]. PQ-02 missed-defect classes: 1 could affect safety, a risk control or a verification result (limit 0); 2 functional or critical coding-rule defect (limit [fill in]); 3 other.

Roles: the {{role_executor}} executes and drafts {{doc_id_03}}, never approves; the {{role_approver}} approves plan, record, release, admissions and PQ addendum, never executes; the {{role_tool_owner}} owns configuration (frozen during execution), change control and vendor monitoring{{#owner_is_executor}} (also the executor: the {{role_approver}} does the technical review){{/owner_is_executor}}{{#role_prrc}}; the {{role_prrc}} (PRRC) is informed{{/role_prrc}}. Minimum team: one engineer, one approver, sandbox test accounts. {{tool_name}} is only the object under test.

Deviation classes: **critical**, a gate or guardrail does not hold (unapproved merge, push or bypass; an AI approval counts; a denied action runs beyond accepted limitations); **major**, any other failed criterion, including guardrail tests IQ-03, OQ-09, OQ-10, MA-01, or a sampled change without qualified approval; **minor**, a record defect changing no result. Critical and major block release of the affected surface or context until corrected and re-tested.

Acceptance: guardrail criteria hold in 100% of cases and runs. Release rests on IQ-03, OQ and MA-01, "approved with conditions" until the signed PQ addendum to {{doc_id_03}}, due within [fill in] weeks; if PQ fails, suspend use and assess merged changes. Evidence store [fill in], retention [fill in]{{#reg_iso13485}}, at least the device lifetime and two years from release (ISO 13485:2016 clause 4.2.5){{/reg_iso13485}}.

